Homeworld SDL - Change log

* Homeworld RTX 0.92.0 Public Beta 1 (2026-09-12)

  - Adds expandable Image Reconstruction and Frame Generation selectors using
    the same vertically expanding menu behavior as the main settings screens.
  - Integrates NVIDIA Streamline DLSS-G 2X and AMD FidelityFX frame generation.
    FidelityFX provides the packaged cross-vendor frame-generation option for
    supported AMD and Intel adapters; native Intel XeSS-FG remains visibly
    runtime-gated rather than falling through to a mislabeled implementation.
  - Keeps DLSS/DLAA, FSR Native AA/FSR, and XeSS AA/XeSS-SR reconstruction
    independently selectable from frame generation.
  - Removes duplicate full-scene jitter application in the DLSS path, fixing
    the whole-screen shake observed while DLSS reconstruction was active.
  - Documents the completed 4x modern gameplay-asset pass and its generated
    normal-map policy: normals come from final upscaled opaque color assets,
    while technical masks, UI, and transparent weapon FX remain unmodified.
  - Defines the remaining 1.0 release-candidate work as one small optimization
    pass, opposite-starting-race capture/production support, remaining
    per-mission dust placement, and a final campaign lighting pass.

  - Permanently packages the six authored Mission 1 volumetric dust clouds and
    their distance-fade tuning as the mission's default RTXMAP overlay.
  - Restores the pre-editor simulation and KAS state when switching from the
    Shift+F11 map editor to another authoring tool, preventing Mission 1 (and
    other campaign missions) from retaining a frozen objective state machine.
  - Adds a reproducible 4x Real-ESRGAN weapon-FX texture pipeline covering the
    complete ETG graphics family, preserving source alpha and animation paths,
    then encoding mipmapped BC7 DDS assets without generating normal maps.
  - Makes the legacy particle registry track each replacement DDS's physical
    dimensions separately from its vanilla animation coordinate space. This
    prevents alpha/bias FX passes from copying a 4x surface into a 1x buffer,
    which previously caused a crash when Scout muzzle effects first rendered.
  - Keeps off-screen ships, derelicts and gameplay asteroids in the DXR
    shadow-only scene within the configured maximum shadow distance,
    eliminating shadows that vanished merely because their caster crossed the
    raster camera edge. Dense asteroid fields use their cheapest real mesh LOD
    for these shadow-only instances rather than duplicating authored LOD0 cost.
  - Corrects Mission 6's broader asteroid RenderList handling: asteroid shadow
    inclusion now follows the final camera-frustum visibility result, closing
    the gap where a rock was listed for raster processing but rejected before
    either visible geometry or shadow-only geometry was submitted.
  - Replaces the off-screen asteroid shadow fallback's unrelated retail GEO
    with the exact source-owned modern asteroid triangle mesh and matching
    authored LOD, submitted under a shadow-only DXR instance mask.
  - Fixes effectively dark short-projectile weapons (including Kushan Assault
    Frigate cannons) by deriving useful bounded light range/energy from firing
    hull scale and weapon damage instead of tiny projectile visual length.
  - Audits standard gun paths across fighters, corvettes, frigates, destroyers,
    carriers and motherships; adds a hot-ordnance fallback only for legacy gun
    tables that provide a fully black projectile-light color.
  - Separates dedicated weapon-origin and weapon-impact emitters from the master
    FX/Emissive multiplier, making the four endpoint controls authoritative and
    independently testable while beam bodies and other FX retain the master gain.
  - Adds four live, persistent Global Tuning controls for weapon-origin light
    intensity/range and weapon-impact light intensity/range.
  - Makes every gun and launcher event create an independently tunable muzzle
    or launch-point light, including the sustained origin cap of ion beams.
  - Adds collision-driven lights at bullet, beam, and missile impact points so
    illumination no longer depends on optional or LOD-culled impact sprites.

* Homeworld RTX 0.91.3 Public Beta 4 (2026-09-10)

  - Rebuilds volumetric dust as a world-locked FP16 medium. Clouds retain their
    authored position through camera pitch/yaw instead of behaving like
    billboards, sprites, or camera-facing cutoff planes.
  - Adds half-resolution FP16 integration, near/far world-space froxel
    cascades, conservative empty-space traversal, stable depth termination,
    and amortized lighting evaluation for practical frame rates.
  - Fixes copied ship silhouettes, mirrored depth cutouts, view-dependent
    disappearance, black holes, bright hull halos, and temporal ghost fragments
    inside dense dust.
  - Removes analytic crosses and concentric/cylindrical sampling shells at
    extreme contrast. A rotated 3D noise domain, world-anchored march phases,
    and multi-octave noise-displaced boundaries keep shape choices useful for
    authoring without exposing them as obvious rendered shells.
  - Applies high-contrast dust extinction in linear light and rejects residual
    far-plane background depth so hidden background topology stays hidden.
  - Adds global Distance Fade Start and Distance Fade Strength sliders to the
    Shift+F11 volume inspector. Values update live and persist in RTXMAP 9.
  - Preserves editable Mission Key and Custom Lights metadata while returning
    visible campaign backgrounds to the original BTG renderer, restoring the
    authored galaxies, suns, stars, and gradients.
  - Restores original Homeworld planet meshes, material layouts, silhouettes,
    and six-tile UV atlases beneath high-resolution DDS color and regenerated
    normal overrides.
  - Expands packed-texture lookup to derelicts, scaffolds, debris, and other
    mission-only materials.
  - Replaces unrelated round asteroid fallback LODs with twelve decimated LOD
    meshes derived directly from the four authored replacement asteroids.
    Projected-size selection preserves UVs, identity, and gameplay radius while
    preventing Mission 06 fields from drawing full-detail geometry at distance.
  - Improves DDS and normal tooling so literal normal maps are generated from
    final upscaled color sources while protected technical channels and
    mipmapped BC formats remain intact.
  - Retains the new-extract requirement: manually copy legally owned
    `HW_Music.wxd` and `HW_Comp.vce` beside `HomeworldModern.exe`.

* Homeworld RTX 0.91.3 Public Beta 3 (2026-09-10)

  - Delivers the project's largest asset and loading-pipeline update so far:
    every eligible ship except the already-upscaled R1 Mothership now receives
    a four-times-linear-resolution hull restoration, increasing usable hull
    detail to sixteen times the original pixel count per texture.
  - Adds a reproducible ships-only AI restoration pipeline with extraction,
    classification, resume support, validation, and deployment tooling. Hull
    albedo receives generative restoration while team-color masks, emissive
    masks, material data, transparency, and technical maps are protected from
    generative alteration.
  - Converts the runtime ship library to GPU-native, mipmapped DDS: BC7 for
    high-fidelity color, BC5 for tangent-space normals, and BC4 for masks.
    This preserves the restored source detail while reducing runtime upload
    work and improving minification stability.
  - Replaces inconsistent resolution-dependent runtime relief on upgraded
    ships with deterministic, literal tangent-space normal-map files. Legacy
    content without a sibling normal map retains the generated fallback.
  - Fixes rotating-camera normal-map ghosting and jitter by feeding stable
    tangent-space detail through corrected motion, history, and reprojection
    rules rather than allowing transient screen-space relief to accumulate.
  - Keeps mapped normal detail readable outside direct sunlight by separating
    material relief visibility from the primary sun contribution and retaining
    restrained environment/ambient response.
  - Adds `HomeworldTextures.hwt`, a sorted random-access texture container
    memory-mapped by the executable. The current pack contains 18,662 DDS
    entries in approximately 667 MiB and replaces thousands of individual
    filesystem opens during mission loading.
  - Makes the packed texture library authoritative in release builds, avoiding
    a failed loose-file probe for every packed asset. Developers can restore
    loose DDS priority explicitly with `HW_LOOSE_TEXTURE_OVERRIDES=1`.
  - Eliminates the dominant DXR loading bottleneck by assigning canonical
    normalized names to texture payloads and aliasing repeated materials to an
    existing surface record instead of decoding, hashing, comparing, and
    appending the same texels repeatedly.
  - Replaces exact-size DXR surface-atlas growth with geometric capacity
    expansion. This removes quadratic reallocation/copy behavior as the high-
    resolution library is registered.
  - In the instrumented Mission 01 workload, DXR surface registration falls
    from more than 28.5 seconds to approximately 0.28 seconds (over 99% less),
    while unique processed surface data falls from roughly 266 million to 33
    million texels. Archive reads measure about 0.03 seconds and DDS decode
    about 0.68 seconds in the same diagnostic run.
  - Preserves fidelity throughout the loader optimization: no ship resolution,
    mip level, normal detail, texture channel, or compression-quality setting
    was removed to obtain the measured reduction.
  - Adds four replacement asteroid meshes with authored base-color, normal,
    and ORM DDS material sets. Twelve deterministic runtime silhouette variants
    preserve gameplay radii while providing substantially richer geometry and
    surface response.
  - Extends DXR materials to consume authored normal and ORM data, including
    tangent-frame reconstruction, normal-strength control, roughness/metalness
    response, and safe legacy fallbacks.
  - Hardens compressed-texture handling and shared DDS lifetime management so
    repeated registry/material references reuse decoded or compressed payloads
    without dangling ownership or redundant work.
  - Adds DirectXTex as a pinned build dependency and provides a native
    `ship_texture_dds` conversion helper used by the documented pipeline.
  - Adds automated tests for ship-texture classification, protected-map
    behavior, path preservation, and validation rules.
  - Expands the README, user guide, editing guide, known limitations, and ship-
    texture authoring guide to document the new assets, formats, normal-map
    behavior, packed runtime, developer override, and recovery workflow.
  - Retains the new-extract requirement: users must manually copy their legally
    owned `HW_Music.wxd` and `HW_Comp.vce` beside `HomeworldModern.exe`. These
    retail archives are never included in the repository or release ZIP.

* Homeworld RTX 0.91.3 Public Beta 2 (2026-09-08)

  - Adds capability-based full-scene reconstruction for all major Windows GPU
    vendors. Auto Native selects NVIDIA DLAA, Intel XeSS AA, or AMD
    FidelityFX Native AA; Auto Quality selects the matching DLSS, XeSS-SR, or
    FSR Quality backend.
  - Adds explicit FidelityFX Native AA plus FSR Quality, Balanced,
    Performance, and Ultra Performance modes, using AMD's signed Direct3D 12
    loader and upscaler runtime.
  - Adds explicit Intel XeSS AA plus XeSS-SR Quality, Balanced, Performance,
    and Ultra Performance modes, including Intel's optimized path and its
    supported cross-vendor shader fallback.
  - Unifies DLSS/DLAA, FidelityFX, and XeSS around the same HUD-less color,
    depth, pixel-motion, jitter, history-reset, and native-resolution UI
    contract. Unsupported explicit modes fail safely instead of interrupting
    presentation.
  - Fixes severe DLSS/DLAA pixelation, diagonal tearing/artifacting, and
    unstable reconstruction caused by mismatched temporal jitter and constant
    buffer layout.
  - Fixes stationary generated-normal shimmer by using depth-aware bilinear
    history reprojection and corrected CPU/HLSL temporal-buffer alignment.
  - Integrates and packages NVIDIA Streamline, AMD FidelityFX SDK 2.3.0, and
    Intel XeSS SDK 3.0.2 runtimes. Bootstrap verifies pinned SDK archive
    checksums and the build copies the required signed DLLs beside the EXE.
  - Updates the video settings UI, command-line switches, README, user guide,
    limitations, third-party notices, and rendered PDF manual for the new
    reconstruction matrix.
  - Keeps vendor frame generation disabled pending separate latency and
    presentation validation. Reactive/transparency guidance remains
    conservative for uncommon legacy translucent effects.
  - Retains the new-extract requirement: users must manually copy their legally
    owned `HW_Music.wxd` and `HW_Comp.vce` beside `HomeworldModern.exe`.

* Homeworld RTX 0.91.3 Public Beta 1 (2026-09-08)

  - Publishes the first packaged Windows x64 beta with source, executable,
    symbols, runtime notices, and a complete user/editing manual.
  - Fixes the path-tracing shimmer/ghost trail reported during beta capture by
    correcting temporal-history validity and preserving stable accumulation.
  - Documents the Shift+F11 map/volume editor, Shift+F12 lighting/shadow
    editor, graphics controls, gameplay options, output formats, and limits.
  - Documents the beta workaround requiring legally owned `HW_Music.wxd` and
    `HW_Comp.vce` beside the executable when first-run verification cannot find
    them through a newly selected installation.
  - Excludes all retail BIG, speech, music, and movie data. A legally owned
    Homeworld Classic installation remains required.

* Homeworld Modern 0.91.3 (2026-08-11)

  - Replaced the unrelated procedural cursor with faithful 8x restorations of
    the original Homeworld cursor sprites, retaining the vanilla cursor/action
    mapping and adding a safe original-LIF fallback.
  - Restored first-run validation of a legally installed Homeworld executable
    and its external `homeworld.big`, voice, and music data.
  - Verified the existing DXR direct-light visibility path keeps each ship in
    the TLAS, enabling both self-shadowing and ship-to-ship shadows without
    changing lighting or material tuning.

* Homeworld Modern 0.91.2 (2026-08-11)

  * Windows build hotfix: the dynamically loaded BC7 upload entry point now
    uses the private `hwGlCompressedTexImage2D` symbol. This avoids a collision
    with modern SDL/OpenGL headers that already declare the core
    `glCompressedTexImage2D` function. Runtime rendering is unchanged.

* Homeworld Modern 0.91.1 (2026-08-11)
 - Restores direct LIF registration for the modern surface cache at mesh-load
   time. Derelicts, Khar-Selim / wreckage, debris, mission-only meshes and
   late-loaded GEO/PEO objects now retain their authored diffuse, alpha and
   emissive texels instead of falling back to a flat pale material.
 - Rebuilds all sixteen campaign skies from their own original EZ01-EZ16 BTG
   mesh, palette, blending energy and stars: 4096x2048 BC7 DDS, 13 mips,
   mission-faithful layout, and no generic replacement galaxy artwork.
 - Adds player-only Harvest Beam and Hyperspace palette controls. Each changes
   the visible local effect and its matching DXR light; authored enemy and
   allied colors remain intact. Harvest beams submit a physical line emitter;
   hyperspace gates, slices and fields submit a bounded surface emitter.

* Homeworld Modern 0.91.0 (2026-08-11)
 - Replaces the visible campaign BTGs with sixteen fixed 8192x4096 modern
   360-degree skies. Original BTG palettes, star placement, background color,
   and dominant-light direction remain the authored reference data.
 - Generates every sky from three-dimensional spherical directions and blends
   detailed astronomical material through seam-free triplanar projection.
   There is no pasted rectangular panel, longitude seam, or UV-pole tunnel.
 - Preserves the campaign's spatial color story: cold blue/violet Kharak and
   Wastelands, dense red Gardens/Cathedral of Kadesh, and the escalating
   yellow-orange radiance of the Galactic Core and Hiigara approach.
 - Keeps the original BTG as an automatic safety fallback only when a modern
   sky asset is absent, malformed, or larger than the GPU texture limit.
 - Raises generated-normal detail to a 0-400% range, restores a visibly
   sculpted 100% clean-install baseline, and strengthens the bounded
   primary-surface relief response without feeding texture normals into
   visibility rays or secondary path bounces.

* Homeworld Modern 0.90.1 (2026-08-11)
 - Corrects the supplied Mission 1 artwork projection after live 1440p review.
   The ordinary wide image is no longer misidentified as a 360-degree
   equirectangular panorama or wrapped through UV-sphere poles.
 - Restores the complete original Mission 1 BTG environment and overlays the
   artwork on a 140-by-70-degree curved directional panel in the authored
   opening direction. An eight-degree smooth perimeter reveals the BTG with
   no rectangular edge, rear seam, or polar star-tunnel distortion.
 - Maps the full 4096x2048 image into the useful view sector, raising effective
   1440p texel density from roughly 1024 to 2600 horizontal source pixels while
   preserving its bright-star environment and god-ray contribution.
 - Retains the 0.90.0 Kharak mesh, albedo, renderer, lighting, FX, UI, dossier,
   multiplayer, loading, cursor, and frame-generation behavior unchanged.

* Homeworld Modern 0.90.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Promotes the project to feature-complete beta status and freezes the
   approved path-lighting, material, generated-normal, trail, and FX look.
 - Replaces the multiplayer connection screen with a responsive native UI
   and scales all legacy multiplayer screens from their full atom envelope.
 - Adds a high-resolution procedural cursor and texture-backed HSV/value
   livery picker with RGB, HSV, and hexadecimal readouts.
 - Repairs dossier firepower and coverage by using the original live ship
   statistics calculators instead of uninitialized cache fields.
 - Rebuilds single-player loading around official mission artwork, real
   staged progress, and explicit D3D12 presentation to eliminate the stale
   blue frame that previously cleared only after Alt-Tab.
 - Adds off-by-default Universal 2x frame generation for NVIDIA, AMD, and
   Intel D3D12 adapters; the 3D scene is interpolated before exact current UI
   composition.
 - Isolates god-ray seeding to the detected mission-background emitter,
   increases occlusion sampling, and prevents stars/nav lights from becoming
   repeated radial bands at maximum strength.
 - Applies the player-only nav-light override to both the DXR emitter and the
   visible authored sprite.
 - Replaces Mission 1's BTG dome with the supplied 4096x2048 panoramic star
   field; its authored bright star is the sole god-ray/environment source and
   redundant procedural stars are suppressed.
 - Replaces intact Kharak's low-poly world draw with a 36,864-triangle sphere
   and a generated 4096x2048 desert-planet albedo. The scarred Mission 3
   story-state remains on its distinct original asset.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.6 (2026-08-10)
 - Replaced the oversized three-band engine ribbon with a nine-shell feathered
   plume. Screen-coverage growth is tightly capped, additive energy is spread
   through low-alpha layers, and the near-white core is restrained; existing
   engine/nozzle coordinates, axes, orientation, color overrides and glow
   billboard placement remain unchanged.
 - Added a live, non-pausing lighting editor on Shift+F12 with immediate
   controls for mission-environment light, authored HSF lights, FX/emissive
   light, generated-normal strength, surface reflectivity/roughness and
   path-light exposure. Values persist in the existing options file.
 - Added stable primary-hit environment/direct specular response to generated
   normals without allowing texture detail to steer visibility rays or
   secondary bounces. This restores readable reflective panel relief while
   retaining the camera-motion flicker fix.
 - Synthesized the missing CSM_Info atom at runtime because the shipped
   RightClickMenu FIB contains no dossier control. SHIP DOSSIER now appears for
   every non-empty selection regardless of right-click position.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.5 (2026-08-10)
 - Replaced the LOD-dependent line/pyramid engine trail with a deterministic
   three-layer plasma ribbon at every distance. Moving engines retain a
   colored halo, bright plume, near-white core, and visible nozzle bloom; the
   chosen player emission color also feeds point and line-shaped DXR lights.
 - Made the tactical right-click menu selection-driven: it opens anywhere in
   the viewport while ships are selected. Its Ship Dossier action opens a
   crisp right-docked Fleet Archive panel with group context, live loaded ship
   statistics, and original-manual-derived role summaries.
 - Separated mission-dome capture from planet/world rendering and made the
   god-ray march consult the complete raster world as an occlusion mask.
   Kharak can no longer become a false sun and shafts no longer composite
   through visible ships, planets, or other world geometry.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.4 (2026-08-10)
 - Fixed the symbol-confirmed RenderNAVLights access violation at RVA 0xF3879.
   The legacy renderer also passes Derelict objects through this function using
   the layout shared with Ship through navLightInfo; the player-only override
   now verifies OBJ_ShipType before touching Ship-only ownership data and uses
   safe local-player pointer identity.
 - Kept the hue/saturation chart at reference brightness so black or near-black
   selected colors cannot make the selectable palette appear absent. The value
   ramp still supplies the full unrestricted brightness range down to black.
 - Diagnostic run archives now carry their exact executable and PDB alongside
   the minidump, eliminating a separate symbol-upload step for later crashes.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.3 (2026-08-10)
 - Decoupled emissive engine trails from hull-paint brightness. Unrestricted
   black hulls no longer produce black/invisible ribbons or zero-energy DXR
   lights, and translucent trail geometry receives a resolution-aware minimum
   screen width without restoring N-LIPS to ship models.
 - Replaced the legacy two-color picker with a native responsive fleet palette
   for hull base, stripe/marking, engine emission, and navigation lights.
   Engine emission drives both raster FX and DXR lighting. Navigation overrides
   affect only the local player's ships; authored colors remain the default.
 - Routed legacy HFF text through a final-pixel Windows font cache and replaced
   scaled LIF mouse cursors with code-native vector cursors for crisp output at
   modern resolutions.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.2 (2026-08-10)
 - Removed the legacy 150/255 HSV brightness floor from the primary ship-color
   picker. Both primary and stripe colors now permit the full value range down
   to true black while retaining safe zero-bound slider clamping.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Rebuilt the Build, Research, and Launch manager docks from named,
   independently positioned regions. Queue counts, decrement/increment arrows,
   costs, totals, scrollbars, and action buttons can no longer overlap; legacy
   raster titles and button captions are replaced by scalable code-rendered
   typography over the supplied official-art fleet plate.
 - Added a native responsive Gameplay screen and an Unlimited Strike-Craft
   Fuel option. It defaults off, is ignored in multiplayer, and changes only
   fuel depletion/refill state without touching orders, AI, attack passes,
   docking, ship statistics, or save-game rules.
 - Moved manager lists and headings to larger original Homeworld font faces and
   added a bounded generated-relief response so texture-derived normals remain
   visible under neutral lighting without changing shadow offsets or secondary
   ray directions.

* Homeworld Modern 0.12.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Removed the DXR whole-GPU fence from every frame. Each swap-chain slot now
   owns its instance/light/motion uploads, shader table, TLAS scratch, and TLAS,
   so CPU submission waits only when reusing that completed frame slot.
 - Enabled in-place TLAS update builds when BLAS topology is unchanged while
   retaining full rebuilds for topology changes. Upload resources are
   persistently mapped, capacity-grown, and reused instead of allocated and
   mapped every frame.
 - Cached ranked texture-emissive light prototypes per material variant.
   Per-frame work now transforms cached points and uses partial selection for
   the global light budget instead of rescanning and sorting every triangle.
 - Skipped background and world-only compatibility readbacks when DXR, AA, and
   dependent post effects are disabled. Added 600-frame telemetry for all
   OpenGL readbacks, DXR CPU staging, TLAS refits/builds, and upload allocation
   counts to guide the native-raster optimization milestone.

* Homeworld Modern 0.11.4 (2026-08-10)
 - Removed disk persistence for the D3D12 driver pipeline-library blob after a
   captured second-launch access violation showed D3D12Core reading invalid
   memory while loading it. The safe versioned presenter-shader bytecode cache
   remains enabled, and the single presenter PSO is rebuilt at startup.
 - Added DXBC signature and declared-size validation before accepting compiled
   presenter shaders from disk; malformed entries are deleted and recompiled.

* Homeworld Modern 0.11.3 (2026-08-10)
 - Corrected two MSVC-specific startup-splash compile failures: the Win32
   `LONG` client width is now converted before integer template comparison,
   and the Unicode cursor loader receives an explicitly wide resource ID.

* Homeworld Modern 0.11.2 (2026-08-10)
 - Moved the vcpkg manifest installation tree out of the source build folder
   and into the shared no-space dependency directory. FFmpeg's configure step
   receives the installed-library directory in its linker flags, so keeping
   only `VCPKG_ROOT` free of spaces was insufficient for source trees under a
   normal game folder such as `HW1 RTX`.
 - Added `-VcpkgInstalledRoot` for explicit no-space overrides while leaving
   the source tree and final executable in their familiar locations.

* Homeworld Modern 0.11.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Moved the default vcpkg checkout to the shared, no-space
   `%LOCALAPPDATA%\HomeworldModernDeps\vcpkg` path. FFmpeg 9.0 explicitly
   rejects a build-tree path containing spaces, which prevented builds from a
   normal game folder such as `HW1 RTX`.
 - Made the build script reject/fall back from stale spaced `VCPKG_ROOT`
   values and added an explicit `-VcpkgRoot` override for custom no-space
   dependency locations.

* Homeworld Modern 0.11.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Replaced the temporary generated menu image with a curated interface-art
   system composed only from the supplied official Homeworld concept archive.
   Main, campaign, fleet, systems, and archive contexts use deterministic
   plates, and the live UI now uses Homeworld's Eurosecond and Eurose
   Condensed faces.
 - Added a native Windows startup splash using the official galaxy-map and
   ship artwork. It opens before renderer initialization, reports real loading
   stages and progress, and closes when the game enters its main loop.
 - Enabled FFmpeg-backed Bink decoding by default. Original `.bik` campaign
   animatics now render at their encoded aspect/frame timing, preserve scripted
   speech and subtitles, show their first frame, and can be skipped by input.
 - Added a persistent per-user D3D shader-bytecode and pipeline-library cache
   under `%LOCALAPPDATA%\HomeworldModern\ShaderCache`, with versioned shader
   and adapter keys plus automatic invalid-cache fallback.
 - Stabilized DXR camera motion independently of generated normals: repeated
   meshes are paired with the nearest unmatched previous instance instead of
   render-list index, path samples are screen-stable, temporal reuse remains
   depth validated during zoom, and indirect diffuse energy was reduced.
 - Made each extracted package own its `.deps\vcpkg` checkout by default so a
   stale user-level `VCPKG_ROOT` cannot redirect a new source release.

* Homeworld Modern 0.10.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Stabilized generated texture normals with a Sobel-smoothed source, a
   30-degree relief ceiling, and a lower 45% default. High-contrast paint and
   single texels no longer turn into near-vertical light-catching facets.
 - Separated shading detail from transport geometry. Generated normals affect
   primary surface lighting only; geometric normals now control shadow-ray
   offsets, secondary hits, and diffuse bounce directions, removing camera-
   motion sparkle and self-shadow popping.
 - Bounded and attenuated indirect diffuse return before each recursion and
   narrowed the final hybrid light modulation. Rare emissive/direct samples no
   longer pump exposure across an entire ship while authored emitters remain
   visible.

* Homeworld Modern 0.10.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Made Windows bootstrap ignore a stale persistent VCPKG_ROOT that lacks the
   CMake toolchain and create a repository-local checkout instead. Fresh source
   folders no longer bootstrap one dependency tree and build against another.
 - Replaced the one-bit DLAA control with Off, cross-vendor FXAA, native DLAA,
   and NVIDIA DLSS Quality, Balanced, Performance, and Ultra Performance.
   Streamline's own optimal-size query selects the internal DXR lighting
   resolution; the compatibility world and final interface remain native.
 - Added a 5x5 depth-aware spatial path-light filter and corrected temporal
   history validation to compare against reprojected previous-frame depth.
   LIF surface channels now sample bilinearly, reducing stochastic speckle and
   blocky texture modulation while preserving authored color and silhouettes.
 - Captured mission backgrounds separately from ships, engines, trails,
   weapons, and UI. Environment radiance and god-ray source detection now use
   only that background image, preventing moving effects from becoming false
   suns. Shaft energy is normalized and geometry-attenuated to prevent a
   full-screen white wash.
 - Changed BTG and D3D presenter sampling from nearest to linear and added a
   fixed scene-only sub-LSB dither. Smooth nebula and sky gradients show much
   less 8-bit color banding without animated noise or changes to UI pixels.
 - Accumulated every SDL wheel delta and applied all queued notches through an
   exponential camera zoom. Free-spin and fast wheel gestures no longer become
   steppy or lose most of their movement between rendered frames.

* Homeworld Modern 0.9.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Made every optional post effect truly opt-in: chromatic aberration, motion
   blur, film grain, and god rays now all initialize at 0%, and the renderer
   prints the exact live percentages when settings are applied.
 - Added logarithmic per-pixel depth to the path-history record and reject
   reprojected samples from a different surface. Moving pixels now retain far
   less history, preventing the temporal denoiser from resembling motion blur
   while preserving stable-camera noise reduction.
 - Replaced flat overlay grain with luminance-dependent response-controlled
   monochromatic grain. Deep blacks and highlights are protected while the
   selected strength is concentrated through photographic midtones.

* Homeworld Modern 0.9.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Superseded FEMan's visible menu composition with a code-native responsive
   shell covering front-end, campaign, tutorial, multiplayer, settings,
   in-game menu and modal screens. Existing callbacks, lists and game state are
   retained as the functional control layer, so the replacement does not break
   clicks or screen transitions.
 - Added full-screen, in-game panel and modal layout templates that recompute
   from the active output size. Legacy decorative LIF regions are suppressed;
   shared manager, taskbar, list, button, slider and text-entry controls use the
   replacement visual system.
 - Added packaged, text-free interface artwork derived from the supplied
   Homeworld visual references. It is aspect-fill cropped at runtime and loaded
   relative to the executable, with source-tree and working-directory fallbacks.
 - Anchored the Info/task bar to the physical bottom edge at every output size,
   suppressed obsolete off-canvas taskbar atoms, and rebased cached scrollbar
   thumb geometry when responsive regions move. This removes the isolated amber
   rectangle left behind by the original absolute-coordinate scrollbar code.
 - Added motion-reprojected path-history denoising with radiance clamping. Camera
   and object movement no longer resets the path history every frame, removing
   the unintended one-sample grain/noise seen during normal gameplay.
 - Added scene-only Video controls for chromatic aberration, motion-vector blur,
   intentional film grain, and god rays. Motion blur and grain default off; all
   four preserve the native UI composite and persist in Homeworld.cfg.
 - Made every mission's captured background an environment-radiance source for
   path tracing. Its bright-field centroid also drives the god-ray scatter pass,
   so authored suns and nebulae determine the shaft origin.

* Homeworld Modern 0.8.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Fixed code-owned UI clicks being consumed by their own modal base region.
   Main and Video now use a full-screen interactive child processed before the
   modal parent clears events intended for lower screens, restoring clicks,
   wheel adjustments, and their selected actions without input passthrough.

* Homeworld Modern 0.8.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Replaced the legacy main-menu composition and Video Options screen with
   responsive code-native interfaces. The old decorative LIF atlas is bypassed
   across shared buttons, toggles, fields, lists, sliders, panels and menus.
 - Added real Video controls for window mode, resolution, refresh, frame cap,
   UI scale, DXR enable, path bounces, stochastic samples, generated-normal
   strength, FX emission, DLAA, brightness and effect density.
 - Added a progressive diffuse path integrator with one to three radiance
   bounces, one to four new samples per frame, emissive hits, Russian roulette,
   alpha-tested traversal, generated LIF normals and accumulation reset.
 - Added signed NVIDIA Streamline 2.12 DLAA integration. DXR supplies native
   depth and motion guidance; the interface is composited after DLAA so text
   and controls remain sharp and do not enter temporal history.
 - Reworked the shared HUD/manager palette around matte ink, paper, cool signal
   lines and a restrained amber state accent. Right-docked B/L/R managers and
   the persistent Info manager retain their modern interaction policy.

* Homeworld Modern 0.7.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Replaced object-centred emissive proxies with per-triangle GEO material
   records, authored UVs, and the actual LIF visible/emissive texels. Closest
   hits now evaluate the mapped surface instead of one averaged object color.
 - Added alpha-tested any-hit shaders to primary and shadow rays, allowing
   cutout ship surfaces to transmit rays according to their authored texture.
 - Importance-ranked emissive triangle samples now cast light from exact
   transformed surface points while retaining authored map and dynamic lights.
 - Added exact active navigation-light emitters from their MEX positions,
   ship coordinate systems, flash state, color, size, and current fade.
 - Captured a world-only compatibility frame before regions/UI draw. The
   presenter compares it with the final frame and leaves changed UI pixels
   untouched by the DXR lighting composite.
 - Fixed the x64 LIF loader's packed-source allocation leak so material-atlas
   inspection does not retain an extra full copy of every loaded texture.
 - Defer unresolved shared LIF aliases until the classic texture-registry
   refresh has produced their physical backing paths. A nonfatal existence
   guard prevents alias-only names from ever reaching `fileSizeGet`.
 - Navigation, glow-map, engine, muzzle, weapon, beam, explosion, and other
   FX cast-light contributions all obey the existing global FX light slider.
 - Expanded muzzle-flash reach from an ineffective three-unit minimum to a
   short owner-scaled 24-160 unit pulse, with a fast intensity envelope, and
   prioritized transient weapon emitters when the DXR light budget is full.
 - Moved muzzle lighting to the authoritative projectile-spawn event. Scout,
   corvette, capital-ship, and missile weapons now submit their exact barrel-
   tip position independently of optional ETG artwork, and retain a bright
   120 ms pulse across DXR frames so rapid flashes cannot be missed.
 - Removed the original 10,000-20,000-unit render-list limits and distance
   fades, and gave the main gameplay camera an infinite-far projection. True
   frustum culling remains active, so off-screen objects cost no draw calls.
 - Prevented blended engine glows, distance-faded meshes, depth-write-disabled
   effects, and wireframes from becoming opaque DXR silhouettes. Planet/world
   draws using the alternate background projection are also excluded from the
   main-camera acceleration structure, eliminating displaced distant ghosts.
 - This remains hybrid direct lighting with hard shadows. Reflections,
   indirect GI, denoising, and multi-bounce path tracing are not yet active.

* Homeworld Modern 0.6.1 (2026-08-10)
 - Fixed the DXC Shader Model 6.3 build by renaming a closest-hit local that
   collided with HLSL's reserved `triangle` primitive modifier.

* Homeworld Modern 0.6.0 (2026-08-10)
 - Added the first live DirectX Raytracing hybrid-lighting pass. The renderer
   compiles its Shader Model 6.3 library with DXC, caches a BLAS for each GEO
   polygon object, rebuilds the TLAS from the exact visible object transforms,
   and dispatches primary and shadow rays at the output resolution.
 - Extracted the exact camera-float view matrix and the final OpenGL MODELVIEW
   matrix used by all three mesh paths, preserving animated hierarchy,
   bindings, orientation, scale, and the existing engine-glow coordinates.
 - Made all HSF ambient/distant/point/spot records, dynamic engine/muzzle/
   weapon/beam/explosion emitters, and self-lit ship materials feed the live
   ray-light buffer. Spot cones retain their authored cone-plus-edge falloff.
 - Composited ray-tested direct lighting over the compatibility texture frame,
   preserving original textures, team colors, effects, and interface artwork.
 - Replaced the obsolete Video-menu LOD controls with a live `DXR LIGHTS`
   toggle and `FX LIGHT POWER` slider. The slider affects only cast lighting
   from FX and emissive sources; visible sprites and glow artwork remain.
 - Added `/raytracing`, `/noRaytracing`, and `/fxLightStrength 0-200`, with
   persistent `Homeworld.cfg` values and a D3D12 raster fallback.
 - This is hybrid direct lighting with hard ray-traced shadows. Reflections,
   indirect GI, denoising, physically based materials, and multi-bounce path
   tracing remain subsequent milestones.

* Homeworld Modern 0.5.0 (2026-08-09)
 - Made Direct3D 12/DXGI own visible Windows presentation through a
   triple-buffered flip-discard swap chain. The compatibility OpenGL scene is
   captured into the D3D12 presenter until each draw system is migrated.
 - Added Homeworld 2-style B/L/R manager toggles. Build, Launch, and Research
   now occupy a scaled right-side dock over the live 3D view, and pressing the
   active manager key closes it.
 - Kept the bottom Info/command manager present during normal gameplay while
   retaining the established hide behavior for Sensors and cinematics.
 - Preserved every authored HSF map light for the future DXR scene, including
   its original type, position, orientation, cone, edge, RGB, and intensity.
 - Staged exact world-space light emitters for engine effects, muzzle flashes,
   projectiles, collision-trimmed laser/ion beams, and explosions.
 - Registered GEO self-illuminated/full-ambient ship materials as emissive
   geometry so their real surfaces can light the future ray-traced scene.
 - Ray-traced lighting, path tracing, denoising, HDR output, and DLSS are not
   active in this revision; the new light scene is preserved input for those
   passes rather than a claim that the passes already exist.

* Homeworld Modern 0.4.0 (2026-08-09)
 - Forced every renderable object to its highest-detail LOD0 mesh, including
   the emergency/panic LOD path, so geometry no longer changes with distance.
 - Disabled N-LIPS distance enlargement for ships, attached effects, particle
   systems, trails, and engine glows while preserving model-authored scale,
   world coordinates, transforms, and orientation.
 - Initialize ships at a true 1.0 world-space presentation scale so effects and
   gameplay-side helpers cannot observe the legacy pre-render zero value.
 - Added the first live Direct3D 12 renderer milestone: a hardware device,
   direct command queue, synchronized per-frame command list, and resizable
   RGBA16F HDR render target now run beside the compatibility renderer.
 - Kept OpenGL as the visible presenter. D3D12 rasterized game draws, DXR,
   path tracing, HDR display output, and DLSS remain staged work and are not
   exposed as working options.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.5 (2026-08-09)
 - Fixed the `0xC0000409` startup fast-fail after front-end texture setup:
   the legacy options writer could pass a null `FILE *` to `fprintf` when
   `%APPDATA%\.homeworld` did not already exist.
 - Create the per-user options directory before writing `Homeworld.cfg`, reject
   overlong paths, and handle file-open failures without invoking the MSVC
   invalid-parameter fast-fail handler.
 - Added final-stage markers around primitive rendering, settings application,
   menu music, and main-screen activation.
 - Made sanitized Windows builds copy the required AddressSanitizer runtime DLL
   beside `HomeworldModern.exe` automatically.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.4 (2026-08-09)
 - Identified the post-front-end failure as Windows fast-fail `0xC0000409`,
   rather than an archive, fullscreen, GPU, or OpenGL initialization failure.
 - Added per-file front-end loading markers and finer subsystem markers after
   the point reached by the 0.3.3 diagnostic run.
 - Added `-Sanitize` to the Windows build for MSVC AddressSanitizer stack traces.
 - Configured per-user Windows Error Reporting local dumps from the diagnostic
   launcher so security-cookie fast-fails can produce dumps even though they
   bypass the process unhandled-exception filter.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.3 (2026-08-09)
 - Added a Windows diagnostic launcher that captures stdout, stderr, system and
   GPU information, command-line arguments, and the process exit code.
 - Added an unhandled-exception handler that writes a readable crash report and
   Windows minidump to the active diagnostic run directory.
 - Added durable startup-stage markers around archive, timer, task, audio,
   renderer, input, universe, and front-end initialization.
 - Enabled full linker debug information for useful Release-build minidumps.
 - Corrected the legacy archive CRC array indexing so `Homeworld.big` is no
   longer reported under the `Update.big` label.
 - Made the Windows build automatically recover from a stale `VCPKG_ROOT` when
   the repository-local `.deps\\vcpkg` installation is valid.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.2 (2026-08-09)
 - Made `Update.big` explicitly optional when using Homeworld Remastered
   Collection's Homeworld 1 Classic data.
 - Fixed a fourfold under-allocation in the per-archive file-state table that
   could corrupt memory and crash when files came directly from the larger
   Remastered `Homeworld.big` archive.
 - Replaced the hard-coded 13,887-file Remastered archive check with validated
   TOC-layout detection so alternate language and patched archives work.
 - Reject malformed or unreadable optional archives cleanly and report corrupt
   required archives before attempting to load assets from them.
 - Fixed duplicate Windows manifest embedding with Visual Studio 2026.
 - Made the PowerShell build output errors-only by default, with
   `-ShowWarnings` available for warning audits.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.1 (2026-08-09)
 - Added automatic Visual Studio 2022/2026 detection to the Windows build.
 - Replaced the removed vcpkg WinFlexBison port with bootstrap-managed WinGet
   installation and Bison package-data discovery.
 - Made KAS token recognition case-insensitive and enabled WinFlexBison's
   Windows compatibility output.
 - Removed forced UTF-8 decoding of legacy source and generated mission text.
 - Replaced GCC-only arithmetic on `void *` in the x64 font, front-end, mesh,
   animation, NIS, and texture-list conversion paths with byte cursors and
   fixed-width offsets suitable for MSVC.
 - Declared the legacy window-border setting for the SDL renderer.

* Homeworld Modern 0.3.0 (2026-08-09)
 - Added first-profile detection of the primary display's active resolution,
   color depth, and refresh rate.
 - Confirmed borderless desktop fullscreen as the Windows default while
   preserving explicit command-line and saved preferences.
 - Added a resolution-aware logical UI canvas with aspect-preserving centring,
   scalable controls/hit regions, bitmap fonts, and mouse cursors.
 - Added a persistent automatic UI-scale modifier and `/uiScale 50-200`.
 - Corrected viewport and renderer aspect-ratio updates on Windows resize.

* Homeworld Modern 0.2.0 (2026-08-09)
 - Added a native D3D12 adapter and DXR capability probe to the Windows startup
   diagnostics. This verifies the hardware/driver foundation without exposing
   unfinished ray-tracing settings in the game UI.
 - Added a guarded SDL_net CMake option for the legacy LAN path.
 - Added one-command PowerShell bootstrap and build scripts for Windows 11.
 - Added a Windows 10/11 compatibility manifest with per-monitor-v2 DPI,
   long-path awareness, and non-elevated execution metadata.
 - Added an explicit implementation status matrix for modern graphics work.

* Homeworld Modern 0.1.0 (2026-08-09)
 - Added a Visual Studio 2022 x64 CMake and vcpkg build.
 - Added Windows-native Flex/Bison and KAS mission source generation.
 - Added per-monitor DPI awareness and drawable-size resize handling.
 - Added windowed, borderless desktop, and exclusive fullscreen modes.
 - Added custom width, height, depth, refresh rate, VSync, and frame-limit
   command-line controls without changing the fixed simulation clock.
 - Fixed the x64 single-instance mapping handle and exposed the SDL native
   window handle to legacy Windows integration points.
 - Documented the staged D3D12, DXR/path-tracing, and DLSS architecture.

